# Abjuration

<<~ ahu #definition >>

## Definition

The domain of protection and negation — barriers, wards, dispelling, raising thresholds against a crossing.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #activation >>

## Activation

Orients a module toward **defense**: it blocks, deflects, or unmakes rather than creates. Often runs `hook/sustained` or `hook/imbued` to hold a protection up over time.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #interaction >>

## Interaction

Pairs with `function/barrier` and `function/ward`. Counters offensive crossings; meets the `ecm` negate/suppress modes as the defensive side of the same exchange.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #filters >>

## Filters

```text
[tag[lar:///ha.ka.ba/@sdm/components/domain/abjuration]]                       all abjuration modules
[tag[lar:///ha.ka.ba/@sdm/components/domain/abjuration]tag[lar:///ha.ka.ba/@sdm/components/function/ward]]   warding abjurations
```

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #aftermath >>

## Aftermath

- Confirm whether "dispel/negate" wants its own function component distinct from `barrier`/`ward`.

<<~/ahu >>

